{"file": "n8n-flows-real/mf-recovery.json", "row": 6, "cells": ["Gate: lets only a real lead id through (the Postgres node returns one empty item when no row matches)", "MarkFailed", "lead_key from MarkFailed", "output 0 (lead id present) to AlertFailed; output 1 not connected (empty item ends)", "none: an IF node with no error output; REMOVED in real-v3 (ADDED sweep replaces it)", "none", "none", "none", "no credential", "n8n execution log (not saved)", "nothing", "ends after one item", "L2b1-1"]}
{"file": "n8n-flows-real/mf-recovery.json", "row": 7, "cells": ["Sends the alert mail 'lead failed ... a person decides' directly after the state is set, once per newly failed lead", "FailedRow output 0", "lead_key from MarkFailed row; recipient from $env.DESK_ALERT_TO, sender placeholder FROM_ADDRESS_PLACEHOLDER", "one plain-text mail to the alert address; no output to any node", "onError=continueRegularOutput: if SMTP fails or hangs the error is swallowed, the row is already final (failed) and excluded from recovery, so the alert is never sent again = lost notification (REMOVED in real-v3, replaced by AlertClaim/AlertSend/AlertMark sweep; V3-README says so, diff agrees)", "none: no marker records that the alert was sent; sent at most once per run of MarkFailed, and MarkFailed cannot match the row again", "none (sends mail only)", "smtp credential name mf-mail-smtp (id placeholder SMTP_CREDENTIAL_ID); env name DESK_ALERT_TO", "runs as the n8n instance owner with the named credential; no per-flow identity (UNVERIFIED: runtime account)", "SMTP server log (UNVERIFIED), n8n log not saved", "alert mail '[demo] Lead desk: lead failed <lead id>' to the alert address, or nothing if SMTP failed", "ends after one send attempt; no retry (retry fields none)", "L2b1-1"]}
