{"file": "n8n-flows-real-v3/mf-recovery.json", "row": 6, "cells": ["Alert sweep step 1: claims up to 5 rows in state unknown or failed with alert_sent=false and an expired alert_until, sets a token and a claim window of 60 s x (1 + min(attempts,4)) (60 to 300 s)", "Every30s (third branch, parallel to MarkFailed and ClaimStuck)", "none (reads mf_leads by condition)", "rows (lead_key, state, alert_token) to AlertRow; empty item when none", "onError=continueRegularOutput: a database error is swallowed, nothing is sent this tick, next tick retries (late, not lost)", "lead_key + alert_token; FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED so two recovery copies cannot take the same row; alert_sent only set after a send", "mf_leads (Postgres): alert_until, alert_token, alert_attempts (columns exist only in n8n-flows-v3/mf_leads.sql, not in n8n-flows/mf_leads.sql)", "postgres credential name n8n-publish-pg (id placeholder PG_CREDENTIAL_ID)", "runs as the n8n instance owner with the named credential; no per-flow identity (UNVERIFIED: runtime account)", "n8n execution log (not saved)", "nothing directly; an alert mail arrives later", "no stop: retried every tick until alert_sent=true; no hard cap by design (V3-README). The 60 s first window is shorter than a slow SMTP answer, so a second alert can be sent (changed in real-v4 to 720 s, diff: CHANGED AlertClaim.parameters)", "L2b1-3"]}
{"file": "n8n-flows-real-v3/mf-recovery.json", "row": 7, "same_as": "same as n8n-flows-real-v4/mf-recovery.json:AlertRow (machine diff identical)"}
{"file": "n8n-flows-real-v3/mf-recovery.json", "row": 8, "cells": ["Alert sweep step 3: sends the alert mail, subject and text chosen by state (unknown or failed)", "AlertRow output 0", "lead_key, state, alert_token from AlertClaim; recipient $env.DESK_ALERT_TO", "success output 0 to AlertMark; error output 1 goes nowhere in real-v3 (real-v4 ADDS edge AlertSend 1 -> AlertBackoff)", "onError=continueErrorOutput: on failure the item leaves by output 1 which is not connected, so the row keeps alert_sent=false and waits for its claim window to end, then AlertClaim retries; no shortened backoff in this version (fixed in real-v4)", "alert_token on the row (AlertMark requires the same token and alert_sent=false); a send that outlasts the 60 s window can produce a second mail", "none (mail only)", "smtp credential name mf-mail-smtp (id placeholder SMTP_CREDENTIAL_ID); env name DESK_ALERT_TO", "runs as the n8n instance owner with the named credential; no per-flow identity (UNVERIFIED: runtime account)", "SMTP server log (UNVERIFIED)", "alert mail '[demo] Lead desk: mail outcome unknown for <id>' or '... lead failed <id>'", "no retry fields; the sweep retries on later ticks with no hard stop", "L2b1-3"]}
